From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:31:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Resource, Navigation, Server and Paint Timing as in
 Blink

Resource Timing reports <img> (initiator "img") and <link rel=stylesheet>
("link", as every engine and WPT do), a parser-blocking script as
render-blocking, the response body's encoded and decoded sizes, its
content encoding and minimised content type, Server-Timing as
PerformanceServerTiming (from the unfiltered headers, dropped by a failed
timing allow check, which also reports transferSize 0), Blink's extra
attributes (contentEncoding, the service worker router fields) in Blink's
order, and a same-origin iframe's document to its container's global.
PerformanceEntry has navigationId; PerformanceNavigationTiming has
activationStart and notRestoredReasons. Paint Timing reports first-paint
and first-contentful-paint, VisibilityStateEntry the initial and changed
visibility states, and supportedEntryTypes lists the registry's types in
Blink's alphabetical order (the event, LCP, layout-shift, longtask and
other types are accepted, with empty buffers). An embedder that reuses a
global can reset its performance timeline.
